    <name>
      <text>12.1 Arithmetic sequences guided towards sum</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Consider the arithmetic (or linear) sequence \({@seq[1]@},{@seq[2]@},{@seq[3]@},{@seq[4]@},\dots\)</p>
<p>1. What is the first term \(a\)?</p>
<p>\(a = \)[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>
<p>2. What is the common difference \(d\)?</p>
<p>\(d = \)[[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>
<p>3. What is the expression for the \(n\)th term? Give your answer in the form \(p + q n\).</p>
<p>\(a_n = \)[[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</p>
<p>4. If you want to add the first \(n\) terms of an arithmetic sequence you can use the formula \[S_n= \frac{n}{2}\big[ 2a+(n-1)d\big].\]</p> 
<p>What is the sum of the first \({@nn@}\) terms?</p>
<p>[[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans4]] [[feedback:prt4]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
